 ## Overview
-Generates a 2D Worley (Voronoi) noise texture to break up smoke silhouettes, updated per frame via compute shader [S1, unofficial]. It differs from its parent [Worley Noise](1726-worley-noise.md) by explicitly incorporating a time uniform to animate the point positions, and from [Voronoise](5519-voronoise.md) by returning raw distance values rather than smoothed vector displacements [G].
+Generates a 2D Worley (Voronoi) noise texture updated per frame via a compute shader to break up smoke silhouettes [S1, unofficial]. It differs from static Worley noise by incorporating a time-based UV offset to create motion, and from 3D procedural volumes by operating on a 2D texture plane, which is then sampled during ray marching [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-- `id`: Thread ID (`uint3`), derived from `SV_DispatchThreadID`.
-- `_NoiseResolution`: Texture resolution (width/height).
-- `_Scale`: UV multiplier.
-- `_Time`: Time uniform.
-- `range`: Neighborhood search radius.
